5. Control Database and Metadata Tables

The "etl_control" database stores the metadata required to select source folders, target databases, source files, and target tables.

5.1 HospitalConfig Table

The table "dbo.HopitalConfig" stores hospital-level configuration.

CREATE TABLE dbo.HopitalConfig
(
    ConfigID       INT IDENTITY(1,1) PRIMARY KEY,
    SourceFolder   VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    TargetDatabase SYSNAME NOT NULL,
    Is_active      BIT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    CreatedDate    DATETIME2 NOT NULL DEFAULT SYSDATETIME()
);

5.2 fileconfig Table

The table "dbo.fileconfig" stores source filenames and target table names.

CREATE TABLE dbo.fileconfig
(
    ConfigID    INT IDENTITY(1,1) PRIMARY KEY,
    filename    VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    TargetTable SYSNAME NOT NULL,
    IsActive    BIT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    CreatedDate DATETIME2 NOT NULL DEFAULT SYSDATETIME()
);

